First Author: Mardini
Title: An explainable machine learning approach using contemporary UNOS data to identify patients who fail to bridge to heart transplantation
Source number: 34  ￼

Very short summary: This study developed explainable XGBoost models to predict failure to bridge to heart transplantation among UNOS Status 2 candidates supported with IABP or Impella. Five key findings were: (1) 4,178 Status 2 patients from 2018–2022 were analyzed, and 12% experienced Status 2 failure; (2) the overall XGBoost model used 19 variables and achieved AUC 0.71 ± 0.03; (3) performance varied by UNOS region, with AUCs ranging from 0.44 ± 0.08 to 0.74 ± 0.01; (4) specificity was consistently high, ranging from 0.75 to 0.96; and (5) the top overall predictors were number of inotropes, creatinine, sodium, BMI, and blood group. Tables 1–2 and Figures 1–2 were directly used for this extraction.  ￼

