	•	Section 4 Comments/Quotes: The study explicitly compared several imputation methods, including “XGBoost’s built-in imputation mechanism,” and Supplementary Table S1 determined the best strategy per model; among the restricted categories, “algorithm handles natively” fits best. Class imbalance was addressed by testing under-sampling, SMOTE, and increased class weights. Preprocessing included removal of correlated features, creation of PAPi, missingness indicators, and categorical encoding. Fixed train/test counts were not reported because evaluation used nested cross-validation folds. Code availability was not stated.  ￼

